Cloud Infrastructure Project 3
Overview

This project demonstrates the setup of a basic AWS cloud infrastructure for a fictional startup called TECH-Start.

The objective was to create and manage AWS resources while implementing role-based access control using IAM.

Technologies Used
Amazon Web Services (AWS)
IAM (Identity and Access Management)
EC2
Amazon S3
Tasks Completed
1. IAM User Groups

Created three user groups:

Developers
DataScientists
Marketing
2. Permissions Management

Assigned permissions according to business requirements:

Group	Permissions
Developers	AmazonEC2FullAccess
DataScientists	AmazonEC2FullAccess, AmazonS3FullAccess
Marketing	AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess
3. User Creation

Created users and assigned them to the appropriate IAM groups.

4. EC2 Deployment

Launched and configured an EC2 instance to host the startup's web application.

5. S3 Storage

Created and configured an Amazon S3 bucket for cloud storage.

Screenshots

All screenshots documenting the project are located in the /screenshots folder.

Knowledge Checks

The project also includes written responses covering:

Availability Zones
AWS CloudWatch vs CloudTrail
AWS Well-Architected Framework
